#let ORTrees = $bold("ORTrees")$
We denote $ORTrees$ the set of rooted tree were children are ordered from left to right (min to max or 1 to $n_T$). Such a tree can be represented using a finite $V_T subset.eq NN^*^omega$ closed under prefixes and such that if $u beta in V_T$ then $forall alpha < beta, u alpha in V_T$. In that case, $max {alpha in NN| u alpha in V_T}$ is the number of children of the subtree $u^(-1) T$. For $T$ a tree we denote $n_T$ the number of children of the root. We can also write $N(x_1,...,x_n)$ the tree with children $x_1,...,x_n$.

We define $T[S]$ the induced tree on $ S$, formally $T[S] = arrow.b S union arrow.t S$. Denote $[n] = {1,...,n}$.

Let $sigma = (sigma_T : [n_T] <--> [n_T])_(T in ORTrees)$ be a familly of bijections of the childrens. We define $sigma(T)$ as applying $sigma$ to every subtree of $T$:
- $sigma(l) = l$ for $l$ a leaf.
- For $T= N(x_1,...,x_n)$ we define
$ sigma(N(x_1,...,x_n)) = (sigma(x_(sigma_T^(-1) (1))),sigma(x_(sigma_T^(-1) (2))),...,sigma(x_(sigma_T^(-1) (n)))). $

For $(sigma_T)_(T in ORTrees)$ such a familly of bijection, define the isomophism $phi_sigma^T : V_T <--> V_(sigma(T))$ as (assuming we represent a $V_T$ as a set of path) :
- $phi_sigma^T (epsilon) = epsilon$
- For $T = N(x_1,...,x_n)$, let $phi_sigma^T (i :: q) = sigma_T (i) :: phi_sigma^(x_i) (q)$ (valid since $q in V_(x_i)$)

A familly $(sigma_T)_T$ is said to be _frontier-preserving_ if for all
$T in ORTrees$ and every prefix-antichain $A subset.eq V_T$,
$
  sigma(T)[phi_sigma^T (A)] = sigma(T[A]).
$


A familly is said to be _subtree-preserving_ if for all tree $T in ORTrees$ we have
$ forall S subset.eq V_T, #h(10pt) sigma(T)[phi_sigma^T (S)] = sigma(T[S]) $

Denote $T scripts(prop)_sigma T'$ if $sigma(T) = T'$. Denote $T prop T'$ if there exists $(sigma_T)_T$ subtree-preserving such that $T scripts(prop)_sigma T'$.

*Lemma* If $(sigma_T)_T$ is _frontier-preserving_, then it is
_subtree-preserving_.

*Proposition* $prop$ is an equivalence relation on $ORTrees$.

